# Line-ending policy.
#
# Without this file, what lands in a working tree depends on each contributor's
# `core.autocrlf`: the same commit checks out as LF for one person and CRLF for
# another, so tooling, diffs and editor behaviour differ per machine for no
# reason visible in the repository. Declaring the policy here makes checkout
# deterministic regardless of local git configuration.
#
# It also closes a real hazard rather than a hypothetical one: nothing today
# prevents a CRLF file being *committed*, and a shell script or hook stored with
# CRLF fails on Linux CI while looking fine to whoever added it. The index is
# currently all-LF (verified with `git ls-files --eol`); this keeps it that way.
#
# Note what this does not do. The CRLF that appears in test fixtures comes from
# `Path.write_text`, which translates newlines to the host's convention at write
# time -- those files are created by Python during a run, never checked out, so
# no attribute here affects them. That is fixed in the code that reads them.

# Normalize every text file on commit and check it out with LF. Git detects
# which files are text; the explicit rules below override it where detection
# would be wrong or where a platform genuinely wants CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Formats whose tooling assumes LF, stated explicitly so detection cannot
# change its mind about an unusual file.
*.jq      text eol=lf
*.json    text eol=lf
*.jsonl   text eol=lf
*.md      text eol=lf
*.py      text eol=lf
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.svg     text eol=lf
*.tex     text eol=lf
*.toml    text eol=lf
*.txt     text eol=lf
*.yaml    text eol=lf
*.yml     text eol=lf
*.js      text eol=lf
*.html    text eol=lf

# Windows shells. PowerShell reads LF fine, but a `.ps1` is edited far more
# often in Windows editors than anywhere else, and cmd's batch interpreter
# requires CRLF outright -- keeping both as CRLF avoids a class of surprise
# that has no upside.
*.ps1     text eol=crlf
*.bat     text eol=crlf
*.cmd     text eol=crlf

# Binary. Normalizing any of these would corrupt them.
*.pdf     binary
*.png     binary
*.pptx    binary
*.docx    binary
*.xlsx    binary
*.jpg     binary
*.jpeg    binary
*.gif     binary
*.ico     binary
*.woff    binary
*.woff2   binary
*.ttf     binary
*.otf     binary
*.zip     binary
